From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer, uiautomationcore: the desktop as programs look for it

Opera's installer, installing its shortcuts, looks for the desktop's icon
list through UI Automation: the root element with a cache request, then a
"Progman" pane by class name and control type, then its SysListView32. It
crashed there (2026-10-04): GetRootElementBuildCache was a stub, and the
installer went on with the NULL root it left.

uiautomationcore: GetRootElementBuildCache and ElementFromHandleBuildCache
give the element with the request's cache built; And conditions are made
(CreateAndCondition and its array forms, and the Or array forms), as Or
conditions are; property conditions compare strings (case-insensitively
with the flag) and ints -- class names, names, control types.

explorer: the shell's desktop has Windows' desktop windows for programs to
find -- "Progman" ("Program Manager") holding SHELLDLL_DefView and its
SysListView32; wallpaper and desktop tools FindWindow("Progman") and send
it 0x52C. Ours draws the desktop itself, so they are one transparent,
click-through pixel, as the desktop's keys window is.

Opera 136 now installs ("Installation succeeded").

Test: test/progman-gate.sh with test/progman-probe.c and
test/uiadesktop-probe.c (mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_PROGMAN, SG_MUTANT_UIA_STUBS).
